+### GP28 external-meter diagnostic builds
+
+The opt-in `sense_probe.conf` image reports firmware `senseprobe-1` and configures
+GP28/ADC2 (Pico physical pin 34) with Zephyr `GPIO_DISCONNECTED` during safe
+initialization. The pinned driver programs disabled pull/input/output controls
+and sets pad isolation. RP2350 isolation latches can retain earlier physical
+pull states, so these register settings alone do not establish analog Hi-Z.
+It does not enable ADC sampling or change the hardware-defined TMUX2819 enable.
+The normal build leaves GP28 untouched. A matched `sense_baseline.conf` image reports `sensebase-1`
+and retains that normal pin behavior.
+
+Build both from the same source with Zephyr 4.4.2 and SDK 1.0.1. From the pinned
+west workspace, with `repo_root` set as above:
+
+```bash
+for sense_variant in baseline probe; do
+  ZEPHYR_BASE=/path/to/zephyrproject/zephyr-4.4.2 west build \
+    -b rpi_pico2/rp2350a/m33 \
+    -s "$repo_root/hardware/firmware/rp2350_debug_helper" \
+    -d "$repo_root/build/dutchmate-rp2350-sense-$sense_variant" \
+    --pristine -- \
+    "-DEXTRA_CONF_FILE=$repo_root/hardware/firmware/rp2350_debug_helper/sense_$sense_variant.conf" \
+    '-DZEPHYR_MODULES=/path/to/zephyrproject/modules/hal/cmsis_6;/path/to/zephyrproject/modules/hal/rpi_pico' \
+    "-DUSER_CACHE_DIR=$repo_root/build/zephyr-cache"
+done
+```
+
+Each image is at its build directory's `zephyr/zephyr.uf2`. Retain both hashes
+and verify each USB firmware label after flashing. Disconnect DUT_VIO power
+and the DUT before entering BOOTSEL or flashing. For an A/B measurement, use
+the same board, meter, wiring and 1.8 V DUT_VIO supply with helper USB powered;
+record DUT_VIO, helper 3V3, GP28 voltage and DUT_VIO current for each image.
+The unloaded 47 kΩ/47 kΩ divider predicts 0.9 V, but the measurement must account
+for meter loading and actual component/pin behavior. A changed voltage after
+the diagnostic supports configuration-dependent loading; it does not establish
+ADC accuracy, TMUX isolation acceptance, or all board acceptance criteria.
+
+The [manufactured-board record](../../validation/phase1_kicad_rev_a.md) keeps
+operator measurements distinct from build and USB observations. Current next
+steps belong only in [development status](../../../docs/development_status.md).
+
+#### Live GP28 pad-control readback
+
+`sense_state_probe.conf` keeps the first probe's pin initialization and adds
+default-off `DUTCHMATE_SENSE_PAD_REPORT`. Each USB epoch reads GP28's live pad
+control and reports `sensepad-1-pXXXXXXXX` in the existing firmware identifier,
+where `XXXXXXXX` is the eight-digit hexadecimal register value. The value is
+read before the epoch starts UART acquisition. ADC remains disabled; there
+are no new protocol fields, commands or capabilities. Stack and pad reporting
+are separate diagnostic configurations.
+
+Build with the same pinned workspace/toolchain/module arguments above, using
+`-d "$repo_root/build/dutchmate-rp2350-sense-state-probe"` and
+`"-DEXTRA_CONF_FILE=$repo_root/hardware/firmware/rp2350_debug_helper/sense_state_probe.conf"`.
+The image is that directory's `zephyr/zephyr.uf2`. Keep the earlier baseline and
+`senseprobe-1` images and hashes for comparison.
+
+Relevant pad masks are ISO=`0x100`, output-disable=`0x80`, input-enable=`0x40`,
+pull-up=`0x08` and pull-down=`0x04`. A reported cleared pull bit is not proof
+that the physical pull changed while ISO remains set. The
+[RP2350 datasheet §9.7](https://pip-assets.raspberrypi.com/categories/1214-rp2350/documents/RP-008373-DS-2-rp2350-datasheet.pdf?disposition=inline)
+describes how isolation latches hold pad controls until ISO is cleared.
+This corrects the earlier assumption that `GPIO_DISCONNECTED` alone guarantees
+an unloaded analog input; actual pad readback and a controlled ISO-release
+measurement are separate evidence steps.
+
+#### Controlled GP28 isolation-release comparison
+
+`sense_iso_probe.conf` adds default-off `DUTCHMATE_SENSE_RELEASE_ISOLATION`
+to the readback configuration. After the same successful GPIO-disconnect
+configuration, it clears only GP28's ISO bit so the disabled pull/output
+controls can reach the pad. Failed GPIO configuration returns before this
+write. Each epoch reports `senseiso-1-pXXXXXXXX`; with the other observed
+controls unchanged, the register is expected to change from `0x192` to `0x92`.
+That expectation is not a physical voltage or acceptance result.
+
+Build with the same arguments, using
+`-d "$repo_root/build/dutchmate-rp2350-sense-iso-probe"` and
+`"-DEXTRA_CONF_FILE=$repo_root/hardware/firmware/rp2350_debug_helper/sense_iso_probe.conf"`.
+Retain the readback-only image and physical baseline. Flash with Pico isolated
+from the helper and DUT_VIO off, verify the reported raw controls, then repeat
+the same off-board GP28-connected divider measurements. This experiment does
+not implement ADC sampling or change the default normal-firmware behavior.
+
